-- SCENARIO: Public Prosecutor v Tan (scenarios/public-prosecutor-v-tan/SCENARIO.md).  Generated by build.py; do not edit.
-- Mr Tan is found holding packets of 4 g of diamorphine in a flat whose key he holds, with a weighing scale.
-- At the station he offers $5,000 to Officer Lim, a Government officer, to lose the exhibit.  The prosecution charges s 5(1) of the Misuse of Drugs Act 1973
-- and s 5(b) of the Prevention of Corruption Act 1960, and relies on his offer as a statement of an accused.

§ `The statements the two Acts make, as the Acts' own scenario files assert them`

`the MDA statement` MEANS `Written Law Procedure Statement` WITH
    `the Act` IS "Misuse of Drugs Act 1973"
    `the Act deems the offence to be an arrestable offence for the purposes of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010` IS FALSE
    `the Act empowers the police to arrest without warrant for the offence` IS TRUE
    `the Act shows the offence as triable by a District Court under that Act` IS TRUE
    `the Act shows the offence as triable by a Magistrate's Court under that Act` IS FALSE

`the PCA statement` MEANS `Written Law Procedure Statement` WITH
    `the Act` IS "Prevention of Corruption Act 1960"
    `the Act deems the offence to be an arrestable offence for the purposes of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010` IS TRUE
    `the Act empowers the police to arrest without warrant for the offence` IS FALSE
    `the Act shows the offence as triable by a District Court under that Act` IS TRUE
    `the Act shows the offence as triable by a Magistrate's Court under that Act` IS FALSE

`a silent Act` MEANS `Written Law Procedure Statement` WITH
    `the Act` IS "Misuse of Drugs Act 1973"
    `the Act deems the offence to be an arrestable offence for the purposes of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010` IS FALSE
    `the Act empowers the police to arrest without warrant for the offence` IS FALSE
    `the Act shows the offence as triable by a District Court under that Act` IS FALSE
    `the Act shows the offence as triable by a Magistrate's Court under that Act` IS FALSE

§ `Tan: the offence under each Act, as the Code treats it`

`the MDA 5(1) charge` MEANS `Jurisdiction Facts` WITH
    `the offence is punishable with death` IS FALSE
    `the offence is punishable with imprisonment for life` IS FALSE
    `the offence is a fine-only offence` IS FALSE
    `the maximum term of imprisonment provided by law, in years` IS 20
    `the offence is under the Penal Code 1871` IS FALSE
    `the First Schedule shows the offence as triable by a Magistrate's Court` IS FALSE
    `the First Schedule shows the offence as triable by a District Court` IS FALSE
    `a law other than the Penal Code 1871 shows the offence as triable by a Magistrate's Court under that law` IS FALSE
    `a law other than the Penal Code 1871 shows the offence as triable by a District Court under that law` IS FALSE
    `the Public Prosecutor has authorised in writing a Magistrate's Court to try the offence in the particular case` IS FALSE
    `the Public Prosecutor applies to the District Court to try the offence` IS FALSE
    `the accused consents, or if more than one are charged together with the same offence, all consent` IS FALSE

`the PCA 5(b) charge` MEANS `Jurisdiction Facts` WITH
    `the offence is punishable with death` IS FALSE
    `the offence is punishable with imprisonment for life` IS FALSE
    `the offence is a fine-only offence` IS FALSE
    `the maximum term of imprisonment provided by law, in years` IS 5
    `the offence is under the Penal Code 1871` IS FALSE
    `the First Schedule shows the offence as triable by a Magistrate's Court` IS FALSE
    `the First Schedule shows the offence as triable by a District Court` IS FALSE
    `a law other than the Penal Code 1871 shows the offence as triable by a Magistrate's Court under that law` IS FALSE
    `a law other than the Penal Code 1871 shows the offence as triable by a District Court under that law` IS FALSE
    `the Public Prosecutor has authorised in writing a Magistrate's Court to try the offence in the particular case` IS FALSE
    `the Public Prosecutor applies to the District Court to try the offence` IS FALSE
    `the accused consents, or if more than one are charged together with the same offence, all consent` IS FALSE

-- MDA 5(1): 20 years is above s 8(1)'s 10, so a District Court may try it only because MDA s 53 says so (s 9(3)(b)); with a silent Act it may not.

#ASSERT `the offence under the Act is an arrestable offence` `the MDA 5(1) charge` `the MDA statement`

#ASSERT `a District Court may try the offence under the Act` `the MDA 5(1) charge` `the MDA statement`

#ASSERT NOT `a District Court may try the offence under the Act` `the MDA 5(1) charge` `a silent Act`

#ASSERT NOT `a Magistrate's Court may try the offence under the Act` `the MDA 5(1) charge` `the MDA statement`

-- PCA 5(b): 5 years, so a Magistrate's Court may try it under s 7(1)(a) although the Act is silent on Magistrates; arrestable because PCA s 32(1) deems it so.

#ASSERT `the offence under the Act is an arrestable offence` `the PCA 5(b) charge` `the PCA statement`

#ASSERT `a Magistrate's Court may try the offence under the Act` `the PCA 5(b) charge` `the PCA statement`

#ASSERT `a District Court may try the offence under the Act` `the PCA 5(b) charge` `the PCA statement`

§ `Tan: the criminal case disclosure procedures (Second Schedule, s 159)`

#ASSERT `the Act's offence is under a law specified in the Second Schedule` `the MDA statement` "5"

#ASSERT `the Act's offence is under a law specified in the Second Schedule` `the PCA statement` "5"

`tried in a District Court, no consent` MEANS `State Court Disclosure Facts` WITH
